Glossary of Key Terms

Term	Definition
Action Functional (A)	A formal mathematical structure, expressed as an integral, from which the RSVP dynamics are derived via a variational principle. It balances energy, meaning, and entropy to define the system's evolution.
Agency Coherence Ratio (Γ)	A metric defined as the mutual information between the scalar field (Φ) and the vector field (v), divided by the entropy of the entropy field (S). It quantifies the coherence and persistence of agency.
Batalin–Vilkovisky (BV) Formalism	A mathematical structure from symplectic geometry used in Article II to govern entropy/negentropy exchange. A core component of the categorical and geometric reformulation of the RSVP plenum.
Bruno's Ark	A mythic cycle described in Article VI of "The RSVP Manifold" that encodes the complete RSVP dynamics in narrative form. It serves as a high-compression projection of the plenum's structure for human cognition.
CLIO (Cognitive Descent for Optimization)	The fifth level of the RSVP stack, modeling intelligence as a descent or optimization process. It uses a loss functional to find optimal cognitive policies that balance entropy, sparsity, and agency flow.
Deck-0 Hypothesis	The proposition that a quasi-latent, slow, global entropy reservoir exists. It acts as a sink for semantic distinctions, encodes a history of the plenum's state, provides stability, and can re-inject entropy as noise.
EBSSC (Entropy-Bounded Sparse Semantic Calculus)	The second level of the RSVP stack, derived from the base RSVP dynamics. It reinterprets the fields as a semantic manifold where inference is constrained by entropy budgets and sparsity priors to be economical.
Entropic Redshift (zRSVP)	A proposed mechanism to explain cosmic redshift as a consequence of cumulative entropy flux over time, offering a falsifiable alternative to the metric expansion of spacetime.
Functor Fields	A concept from the categorical reformulation of RSVP where fields themselves are treated as functors. Functor field collisions represent semantic phase transitions or failures of conceptual coherence.
Lamphrodyne Relaxation	A process of asymptotic smoothing described in Article I, where the entropy field (S) undergoes exponential gradient decay, leading to equilibrium.
Observer Holography	The theory that observation is a lossy projection of the high-dimensional plenum onto an observer's lower-dimensional perceptual manifold. The perceived world is a biased, compressive, and filtered reduction of the true plenum structure.
RSVP (Relativistic Scalar-Vector Plenum)	The foundational layer of the framework, comprising a scalar field Φ (potential/density), a vector field v (flow/agency), and an entropy field S (disorder/budget). Also refers to the entire theoretical stack built upon this plenum.
Scalar Field (Φ)	One of the three core fields. Represents scalar potential, semantic density, physical potential energy, or cognitive load. Its gradients drive the vector field.
Spherepop Calculus	The third level of the RSVP stack, modeling institutions as thermodynamic "spheres." It defines rules for how these spheres maintain internal order and merge ("pop") based on permeability and resistance thresholds.
TARTAN	The fourth level of the RSVP stack, representing memory as recursive lattices of "memory tiles." It also refers to the braided tensor networks used in the categorical geometry of the plenum.
Vector Field (v)	One of the three core fields. Represents directed flow, agency, influence, causal flow, or policy gradients. It redistributes the scalar potential and is modulated by entropy.
Xylomorphic Architecture	A design principle mentioned in Article V related to "Forest Intelligence." It is part of the application of RSVP principles to create stable civic and social architectures.

